<concept id="t00310">
	<title>Tailgate light</title>
	<shortdesc>When an emergency situation such as a vehicle breakdown occurs, open the tailgate and activate it together with the hazard warning lights to alert surrounding vehicles to the emergency situation and help prevent secondary accidents.</shortdesc>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>interior lights
					<indexterm>tailgate light</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>tailgate light</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01973">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01974">
								<image href="images/N_SP327_C08_044_1.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul id="e01975">
			<li>
				<p>When you open the tailgate, the lamp turns on.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When you close the tailgate, the lamp turns off.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<note type="caution" id="e01976">
			<p>Make sure that the tailgate is fully closed.</p>
			<p>If the lamp remains on, it may cause 12 V battery discharge and tailgate damage.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
